data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"The loss has two parts. One is how much router probability each expert receives on average. The\nother is how many tokens each expert actually receives. Their product, summed over experts, is\nsmall only when both are spread evenly. Only the probability part can carry a gradient, because\ncounting tokens is a discrete step."},"hints_note":null}

