data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Compute the softmax of each row of logits. Average each column to get `P`, of shape `(E,)`. For\n`f`, find the top-1 expert of each token, breaking ties toward the lower index, count how many\ntokens chose each expert, and divide by `T`. The loss is `alpha * E * sum(f * P)`. Check the\ninputs first: rank, dtype, `T` and `E`, finiteness, and the type and sign of `alpha`."},"hints_note":null}

