data: {"level":3,"reviewed":{"level":3,"label":"code shape","text":"Use `torch.softmax(logits, dim=-1)` and then `.mean(dim=0)` for `P`. For the top-1 choice, sort each\nrow with `torch.sort(..., descending=True, stable=True)` and take column 0. Pass those indices to\n`torch.bincount(..., minlength=E)`, convert to float64 and divide by `T`. Return `alpha * E` times\nthe sum of the elementwise product of `f` and `P`. That is a 0-dimensional tensor."},"hints_note":null}

